Spec: File System
Purpose:
  Provide Node filesystem adapter operations.

Structure:
  ./file-system.ts: File system adapter implementation.
  ./file-system.test.ts: File system adapter tests.

Owns:
  ./file-system.ts
  ./file-system.test.ts

Must:
  Expose @FileSystem.exists.
  Expose @FileSystem.isDirectory.
  Expose @FileSystem.createDirectory.
  Expose @FileSystem.readFile.
  Expose @FileSystem.writeFile.
  Check whether the provided path exists.
  Check whether the provided path is a directory.
  Create directories only when @FileSystem.createDirectory is called.
  Read bytes from the provided path.
  Write bytes to the provided path.
  Keep parent directory creation separate from @FileSystem.writeFile.
  Inspect a path without following its final symlink through @FileSystem.lstat and resolve existing symlinks through @FileSystem.realpath.
  Atomically replace a file through @FileSystem.writeFileAtomic using a unique sibling temporary file and rename, preserving the preceding destination when replacement fails.
  Keep parent directory creation separate from @FileSystem.writeFileAtomic and clean up its temporary files after failure.
  Remove an explicitly supplied file or directory through @FileSystem.removePath, with recursive removal requiring an explicit option.
  Run a callback under an exclusive filesystem lock through @FileSystem.withExclusiveLock, preventing callbacks using the same lock path from overlapping across processes.
  Reject an already held lock without running the callback or removing that lock, and release an acquired lock after callback success or failure.
  Preserve filesystem error details for callers of the path inspection, atomic replacement, removal, and locking operations.

Depends on:
  Node.js filesystem

Exposes:
  @FileSystem
  @FileSystem.exists
  @FileSystem.isDirectory
  @FileSystem.createDirectory
  @FileSystem.readFile
  @FileSystem.writeFile
  @FileSystem.lstat
  @FileSystem.realpath
  @FileSystem.writeFileAtomic
  @FileSystem.removePath
  @FileSystem.withExclusiveLock
